## [ENT-126] | 2026-11-22 06:14 UTC | Unity | error | ref: game/fleet/wallet.py | see: queue.log ENT-218
What: the leader's deposit into the faction's treasury did not run from 03:12 to 06:09 UTC but once (05:08, refused for a fight); 1,240,781 cr stood in the leader's wallet instead of the treasury (sweep.jsonl; wallet.py sweep --dry-run 06:08 UTC).
Effect: the treasury read 1,664,515 cr while the Recruitment Center's fee is 2,000,000; no credit lost. After the fix the deposit of 1,190,781 cr booked at 06:11 UTC.
Cause: the pass gives up to four gifts first, about 80 s each, and the deposit waits when DEPOSIT_BY (90 s) is used up; the sweep lines by role of 02:05 UTC put 29 ships above their line, so every pass gave four gifts. The job prints only HALT lines, so the waiting deposit printed nothing anyone read.
Fix: commit 1077d775: the leader holding 100,000 cr or more above its line deposits before the pass's gifts; after a deposit refused for a fight the gifts go first again (test failed on the old code first).
Class: a step that runs last in a time-boxed pass starves without a word (a silent wait). Would it have prevented this one: yes, the deposit comes first whenever it is large.

## [ENT-127] | 2026-11-22 06:14 UTC | Unity | error | ref: scripts/fleet-build.sh | see: queue.log ENT-218
What: from 04:53 UTC every `fleet-build.sh test` in a member's copy halted at GATE validate-ids (CalledProcessError of `git ls-files`): commit 32416700 rewrote scripts/validate-ids.sh to list Markdown by git, and a copy made by `fleet-build.sh tree` is no git folder. Seen at 05:42 UTC in my own build; no Admiral's turn ran in between.
