## [ENT-136] | 2026-11-22 14:12 UTC | Unity | error | ref: game/fleet/fill.py | see: ENT-131
What: the cause of ENT-131 found. `fill.claims()` leaves standing work out of every claim, and `routes.standing()` counts a hunt with `gift_to` as standing work while data/fleet/strict-classes-on stands (`routes.gives`). The status of 09:32 UTC ran before the switch went on at 09:35 UTC, the write of 09:57 UTC after it: the two paths never disagreed, the switch moved between them. From 09:35 UTC every hunt claim of Military and Intel was void for the filler, and the hourly pass of 12:39 UTC put a Military hunt in front of a flagship's routes again.
Effect: the command plan held 29 hunts Military (26) or Intel (3) claim, the scout plan several of Military's; each herd carries one side, so the first free ship took it. No ship lost, no credit lost that a record shows.
Fix, done: claims() keeps a claim on a hunt whether or not it is standing work (commit 17cb9c29; its test failed on the old code first); the 29 hunts are out of the command plan (commits 88a2d1e8 and the five before it); the filler's next write offered no claimed hunt (fill.py fill command, 14:15 UTC).
Would it have prevented this one: yes; with the fix the 12:39 UTC pass prints the two hunts as "not offered: claimed by another division".
Class: a switch that changes what a rule means for a second reader (strict classes made hunts standing work; the claim reader trusted "standing means unclaimed"). Each switch's commit should name every reader of the property it changes.

